\newlabel{fig:trust}{{1}{2}{One action produces two records. Left of the dashed line everything is written by the agent and can be rewritten by it; the log-only monitor has no other input, so it sees the claim and reports nothing. Right of the line the kernel witnesses the syscall, resolves who acted and on what, and the correlator emits an edge. The object is identified by device and inode rather than by path}{figure.caption.1}{}}
